{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And He said, His devout ones</b> — And He mentioned the children of Israel. And the word עם is not in construct state to its near word [i.e., לו]; rather its meaning is that 'near to Him' is near to the people. And like it: לאיש חסידך."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 148, :notes {0 "The phrase 'near to the people' (קרוב אל העם) is textually difficult; the argument is compressed and the syntax of the Hebrew is unclear, possibly corrupt. Translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:09.988218022Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}